			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2339678">
									

<p>For one thing, the SH reference is left out in the open as a generic GoI that has said SCP without adding on/hinting on its role with said SCP. A few lines/hints to show a faint tint of connection may help.</p>
<p>Secondly, the e-mails are too informal to be taken seriously. As they are, they feel like an exchange among friends rather than talking about the affairs of their work (which is the context). Since the content of those e-mails are about &quot;training&quot; and handling SCPs, the tone should at least be formal and treat the subject-matter with the seriousness it deserves.</p>
<p>PS. How a procedure modification got screwed over by bureaucratic red tape is at least funny in my eyes. But I'm still downvoting due to informal e-mails that would not fit a work setting.</p>

