			<div class="content" id="post-content-2339709">
									

<p>Edit: From <a href="/mackenzie-glossary">Dr. Mackenzie's Glossary</a>, a cognitohazard is something that is dangerous to sense or percieve, whereas an infohazard is something that's dangerous to know about at all. The more you know!</p>
<p>As for the article&#8230;. I need to think on this one for a bit. The physical anomaly is extremely basic, but I get that that's not important. I think this is very well thought-out, but I'd also be interested to know why it escapes and then wipes any memory of the Foundation. It seems that it was very specifically targeted at creation to get out of Foundation custody, and I'd like to know who did that and why. The connection that the Serpent's Hand possibly did it&#8230; doesn't seem to fit for some reason, for me. I almost feel like they found it that way too. (Edit: I think the reason I feel that way is that it doesn't really fit their motives. &quot;We want our weird object to break itself out while effectively disabling Foundation personnel&quot; feels more like an MC&amp;D or CI thing. If there's more specifics about why the SH made it that way, I would prefer to at least partially know them.) Without a hint of that, this is a bit&#8230; sterile.</p>
<p>No vote for now, possible change after some more digestion.</p>

