														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2339730">
									

<p>&quot;<em>Due to its properties as an infohazard, all but two members of the MTF succumbed to SCP-2414's effects.</em>&quot;</p>
<p>What effects? My understanding of the object is that it will try to convince you it's non-anomalous IF it's in foundation containment, only wiping the foundation from the individuals responsible for freeing it.</p>
<p>Or all but two members viewed it as having nine sides?</p>
<p>I might just not be getting it, but from how it reads to me, the item in only an info hazard while under foundation containment. Which just leaves me wondering why they keep it around at all.</p>
<p>according to the description the faces can be marked through typical methods&#8230; so it's not indestructible?</p>
<p>why not neutralize it? Lots of other skips could in theory be destroyed but aren't because the anomaly is worth researching, not cost efficient to destroy, could create a larger problem ect.</p>
<p>But the only way this SCP is dangerous is if the foundation actually keeps it. It literally appears to do nothing else that would really give the foundation a reason to contain it.</p>
<p>All that being said, it's not bad either, I just feel like it needs&#8230;.something.</p>
<p>An anomalous object which causes containment breaches is a great hook for an object, but it's a hook with no bait.</p>

							</div>

								
					
