			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2339980">
									

<p>I like the concept (its anomalous property is that makes people believe it's non-anomalous, that is a lovely semi-paradox at work), but I can't see how the Foundation manage to contain it in the first place. Once it was put inside the containment chamber, everyone who knew about it being an anomalous object would've wanted to remove it from Foundation custody. They also would've told anyone who hadn't been informed of the object that it was non-anomalous. And if it only displays this anomalous property when in Foundation custody, why was it brought in in the first place?</p>

