			<div class="content" id="post-content-2340033">
									

<p>I like this idea, but I think you've done too much with it. I understand from the above posts that the mindwipe is integral to the story you're trying to tell, but it feels like a tacked on secondary effect.</p>
<p>What I'd like to see is an item that compels you to believe it's non-anomalous, liberate it from containment, then go find some guy on the sidewalk to give it to&#8230; at which point the Foundation employee becomes aware of the fact that they've shown an anomalous object to a member of the public. That'd be a horrifying realization, and it would make more sense with (my understanding of) how the Serpent's Hand operates- they want to bring about awareness and acceptance of the anomalous.</p>

